From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Ferralis <ferralis@generalflash.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:50:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: fillet / chamfer on edges and shell with faces named by
 points (Select:Edges@Point, Face@Point)

An intent lists points on the edges it rounds or chamfers, or on the faces a shell removes
("pts"); the model issues one selection command and the runtime picks the nearest edge or
face for each point, as it does for "at". New family and suite "points" (box with bosses,
pockets, holes; dressups on chosen edges of any of them; shells opening chosen faces).
In WHUCAD's hand-built parts this takes the share whose every feature the goals express from
32 % to 96 %. Every earlier suite keeps its goals (large_ext draws from the earlier families).
TAIGA_TRAIN_ONLY=points generates data for this family alone, to add to an existing data set.
